WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.470
A good doctor does four things.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.870
First, name the illness.

3
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.140
Then find its cause.

4
00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:10.210
Next, say whether a cure is possible.

5
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.760
Last, write the prescription.

6
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:16.340
Buddhists say the Four Noble
Truths follow this pattern.

7
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.560
The first names suffering.

8
00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.680
The second names its cause: craving.

9
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.040
The third says it can end.

10
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:28.960
So if craving causes suffering, what
can a person actually do about it?

11
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.600
In this mission, you'll
explore the Fourth Truth,

12
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.250
called magga, and the eight
spokes of the Dhamma wheel.

13
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.490
Then you'll sort the
eight into three groups,

14
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.490
and test them on real choices people make.

15
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.400
Your mission: find out what the Fourth
Truth asks a person to actually do.
